blavaan 0.3-5 is now on CRAN. In addition to some bug fixes, there are some major changes:

- target="stan" is now default. The underlying Stan approach is also new, and it should be faster and more efficient than the old approach in most cases.

- But the new approach introduces some restrictions on priors. If you need to use distributions other than those listed in dpriors(), then you should use target="stanclassic" (the old Stan approach) or target="jags".

- The blavaan installation is heavier due to the changes. I anticipate more problems with installation than before.

